what real criminal case inspired the  character of Eddie Munson and what does  11 have in common with Luke Skywalker  keep watching for Easter eggs you might  have missed in season 4 Volume 2 of  stranger things but beware there are  spoilers ahead  when speaking with Netflix's tadam The  Duffer Brothers hinted at the fact that  Eddie Munson is inspired by a specific  person who is a Dungeons and Dragons  fanatic and Metal Head just like Eddie a  tweet from Netflix geeked confirmed that  Eddie Munson is Loosely based on West  Memphis three-member Damien Eckles a  writer and artist these days Eccles was  one of three teenagers convicted under  highly dubious circumstances of the 1993  murders of Steve Branch Michael Moore  and Christopher Byers and what the media  considered at the time to be Satanic  rituals Eccles had a tendency for  dressing in black and listening to heavy  metal which led the community to  ostracize him and believe he conducted  spiritual practices with ties to  Witchcraft and Satanism in an interview  about season 4 Ross stuffer said  something we really wanted to get into  this year was the satanic Panic the term  satanic Panic refers to a period in the  80s and 90s when Society began blaming  its various ills on the influence of  heavy metal music and Fantastical  imagery from Escapist entertainment like  Dungeons and Dragons  Advocates of the satanic Panic were  specifically concerned about supposed  satanists harming and sacrificing small  children there's a widely held opinion  that what happened at the daycare was  the devil's handiwork The West Memphis  Three were released from prison in 2011.  Echols went on to become a New York  Times best-selling author and produced a  documentary about his experience when  describing the character of Eddie Matt  Duffer said what's sad about his  narrative is that the people who get to  know him love him and the people who  don't have judged him horribly  it's no secret that the creators of  stranger things love to pay respect to  horror classics with the numerous  references they sprinkle throughout the  series and season 4 is no different at  one point Joyce and Hopper come across a  Russian Lab of tanks filled with demic  organs for experimentation and the scene  is almost identical to one in Alien  Resurrection a 1997 movie that just like  stranger things co-stars Winona Ryder  however The Duffer Brothers didn't stop  there there are several other nods to  the alien film franchise throughout the  season such as Paul reiser's use of the  word kiddo Burke reiser's character in  Aliens also makes frequent use of the  patronizing nickname references to the  Stephen King horror classic carry appear  throughout the season as well like when  Elle gets bullied in front of her whole  school and when Max's happy memory of  the winter ball is ruined by  blood-filled balloons the dupper  brothers have confirmed that when  planning the season they focused a lot  on a Nightmare on Elm Street Hellraiser  and the IT miniseries it also said they  modeled after Pinhead from Hellraiser  and of course Robert England plays  Henry's Father Victor creel which means  vechna's dad is pretty much Freddy  Krueger  those final two episodes Volume 2 are  extremely action-packed but did you  notice a familiar weapon amid all the  chaos as revealed by David Harbor on his  personal Instagram page the sword used  by Hopper to slay the demic organ in the  final episode is actually the same  Atlantean sword famously used by Arnold  Schwarzenegger and the Conan the  Barbarian films Barber describes the  prop as both quote heavy as hell and a  tremendous honor to wield fans also  pointed out some foreshadowing to this  epic sword battle that came in the first  episode of season four when we get a  glimpse of Mike's bedroom a poster for  Conan the Barbarian can be seen hanging  on his wall this tiny Easter egg  probably wouldn't have meant anything to  you prior to the finale episode with  hopper Schwarzenegger himself actually  admitted to still owning the legendary  sword and keeping it in his office when  asked if he still had the sword back in  2010 the actor and one-time governor of  California confirmed that he in fact did  and he plays a vital role in the final  moments of the fight with bekna by  sacrificing himself for the greater good  and what is definitely the most metal  concert in the history of the upside  down Eddie shreds to Metallica in order  to distract the demo bats the song Eddie  performs Master of Puppets is of clear  significance given the way vecna tends  to toy with his victims by forcing them  to relive their worst fears and traumas  mechna is basically a metaphorical  Master of Puppets Metallica actually  reposted the clip on their Instagram  page crazy in the show for how well they  Incorporated the song admit to being  blown away by the final product writing  some folks were able to guess the song  just by seeing a few seconds of Joseph  Quinn's hands in the trailer Eddie's  fate sadly seemed to be written in stone  from his first appearance if you look  closely at Eddie's arms you'll see a  tattoo of bats as well as another tattoo  of hand controlling a puppet on strings  direct connections to the circumstances  of his inevitable death  I didn't run away this time right The  Duffer Brothers sat down with collider  and revealed that they had taken a lot  of inspiration from the Star Wars  franchise Matt Duffer said we have  always wanted to do an Empire Strikes  Back ending we tried to do that with  season four where it's the sense of loss  Star Wars episode 5 The Empire Strikes  Back is known for its shocking ending  where the bad guys more or less Prevail  sadly vechna likewise kinda prevails  when the upside down leaks into the real  world of Hawkins Indiana there's also a  similarity between 11 and Luke Skywalker  both characters abandon extensive  training sessions against their mentors  wishes in order to help their friends in  Luke's case his decision leads to the  loss of his hand and Han Solo being  taken prisoner and elevens her attempt  to intervene in beckton's plans leads to  Max's coma blinding and possible  paralysis but one must not Overlook the  moment when Murray utters one of the  most famous lines from the entire Star  Wars franchise I got a bad feeling about  this  there's no denying that Tom Cruise was  an 80s heartthrob following his roles in  Risky Business and Top Gun it's safe to  say that Crews had a dedicated fan base  back in the day and Nancy wheeler was  most definitely a member not only does  Nancy have a Tom Cruise poster stuck on  her wall as of the very first season and  mentions him on several occasions she  and Steve actually dress up as risky  business characters for Halloween back  in season 2. Robin briefly teases Nancy  about her poster which still hangs on  her wall in season four you have a Tom  Cruise poster that's oh  a Reddit user also pointed out the  visual similarities between Steve from  stranger things and Steve from The  Outsiders played by Cruz clearly Nancy  has a type and we can't blame her when  the gang gets together to plan their  attack on vechna they decide to stock up  on weapons at a store called The War  Zone when Eddie points out an  advertisement for the place we see the  company's logo takes clear inspiration  from the Top Gun logo Mason die who  portrays the unhinged jock Jason did an  interview with the Steve barley show and  explained that Tom Cruise was the main  inspiration behind his character he said  I sat down with the dubber brothers and  producer Sean Levy and they were like  okay Jason is just Tom Cruise from his  80s movies so I just went back and  watched Risky Business Top Gun like all  his 80 movies a week prior to filming  in the final episodes of the Season  viewers learned that there was a large  significance surrounding the number four  not only does it clock chime four times  whenever vechna is about to claim  another victim but he also requires  exactly four victims to enact his plan  in order for the upside down to break  through to the regular Dimension Beckman  needs to create four portals which  ultimately results in the four cracks  seen in the final scenes of the Season  while all of this is explicitly  explained throughout the series there  are some additional references that  aren't as noticeable the main characters  are all split into four distinct groups  the Hellfire gang in Hawkins L and papa  in the training facility Hopper and  Joyce in Russia and will encompanying  California it makes this the first  season where characters fight the main  antagonist simultaneously from different  locations across the globe and other  sides of the dimensional barrier if you  were so inclined you could theorize that  the importance of the number four could  relate to the Four Horsemen of the  Apocalypse though we can only hope more  explanations unfold next season  one of the best parts about stranger  things is dissecting the countless  Easter eggs and background details  scattered throughout for example while  the Hawkins group scrambles to find  music to bring Nancy back from Becca's  mindscape we catch a glimpse of Eddie's  bedroom if you look closely his walls  are packed with posters from various  heavy metal bands ranging from Iron  Maiden Anthrax Judas priests Slayer and  Creator proving he is a true Metalhead  an example of subtle symbolism occurs  during the moments of Brenner's death in  the desert as a camera pans over him he  can be seen in a crucifix pose most  likely mirroring the christ-like way in  which he viewed himself however the  camera then flips the image upside down  in order to evoke the evil that Brenner  truly created by bringing becna into  this world when the Hawkins kids go to  the war zone to stock up on weapons they  quickly pass by a bulletin board covered  with wanted posters for all the members  of hellfire club showing that most of  the Town had succumbed to satanic Panic  by this point during the same visit  Robin catches a glimpse of her school  Crush Vicki who is sadly getting cozy  with some guy meanwhile there are  uncanny similarities between Vicky's  wardrobe and the look of Molly  ringwald's character in 16 Candles which  would have been released about three  years earlier which could imply that  Vicky is a John Hughes fan check out one  of our newest videos right here plus  even more Looper videos about your  favorite movies and TV shows are coming  soon subscribe to our YouTube channel  and hit the Bell so you don't miss a  single one  foreign
 

